# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The frontend needs NO configuration to deploy.
#
# The API's location and the Cloudinary cloud name are NOT here — they are in
# deploy.config.js, which is the one place they live (this file is gitignored,
# so it cannot hold production config anyway).
#
# Copy this to .env and leave it exactly as it is.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Leave EMPTY — in development AND in production.
#
# Empty means the browser calls /api on its own origin. In development vite's
# proxy forwards it (deploy.config.js -> API_DEV); in production Vercel's
# rewrite forwards it (deploy.config.js -> API_PROD). Either way the refresh
# cookie stays first-party and there is no CORS preflight.
#
# Set this ONLY if the browser must call the API on another domain directly.
# Then the backend also needs COOKIE_SAMESITE=none — and be aware Safari
# blocks third-party cookies outright, which logs those users out every 15
# minutes when the access token expires. The rewrite avoids all of that.
VITE_API_URL=
